P Address (The Road Map / Building Address):

Tells the network where the building is.

IP does not care if the building is on fire, if anyone is inside, or if the package got dropped in the mud. Its only job is routing from Point A to Point B.

TCP Connection (The Phone Call / Agreement Between People):

Tells the applications how to talk reliably.

Once the road exists (thanks to IP), TCP makes sure both computers agree to talk, numbers every piece of data, and asks for confirmation (ACK) so nothing gets lost.
